# Allowlist, not a denylist. infra/Dockerfile COPYs exactly the paths un-ignored below;
# everything else in the repo root is build scratch (deps/, emsdk/, qt-src/, build-*/ --
# tens of GB on a build machine) that would otherwise be shipped to the Docker daemon as
# build context on every single build.
#
# A denylist loses this race: it has to be updated every time someone adds a new scratch
# directory, and the cost of missing one is silent and invisible. Here the failure mode is
# inverted -- add a COPY without adding it below and the build fails immediately, loudly.
*
!infra/nginx.conf
!play-gui
!LICENSE
!NOTICE
!LICENSES
!tools/patch-freecad-js.py
